Build 1054 — 2026-08-06
- Deleting an account now signs that person out. This is the headline fix. When
  an admin deleted an account, the person kept using the app as though nothing
  had happened. Two things were wrong. The check that runs when the app opens
  read the member's profile, and when the profile was GONE it treated that the
  same as a lookup that had merely failed — and deliberately kept them signed
  in. And the live guard that ejects a banned or suspended member listened only
  for a profile being CHANGED, so it was completely blind to one being DELETED.
  Both are fixed: a deletion now ends the session on the spot if the app is
  open, and on next open otherwise, and the person is told the account has been
  removed rather than being dumped out with no explanation.
- Photographs are read once, and only once. Members were hitting "Failed to
  create post" and could not publish at all. Every recorded failure came from
  the installed app and none from the website. The pipeline was going back to
  the phone's file up to five separate times — once to show the preview, twice
  to security-scan it, and twice more to make the full-size and the thumbnail.
  Now the photograph is read a single time when it is chosen, and every step
  after that works from that one copy. If the phone ever does refuse to hand a
  photograph over again, the post recovers from the copy instead of failing.
- When something does go wrong, it now says what. Failures used to reach members
  as unreadable text like `non-Error thrown: {"isTrusted":true}`. Every failure
  in the app now carries a code, the stage it happened at, the file type and
  size, the Android version and the device — so a problem reported once can
  actually be found and fixed instead of guessed at.
- Members' own words are never recorded. Comment moderation used to print the
  actual text of a comment into the phone's log every time one was blocked, and
  the moderation reply — which repeats the comment back — was logged too. Both
  now record only the length and which rule matched. Search terms and captions
  are treated the same way.
- The diagnostic tool that was running on every member's phone is gone. A
  developer tool intercepted every network request for the first eight seconds
  of every visit, read every response in full just to measure it, and printed a
  report into the phone's console. It now runs only during development.
- A page that fails to load now reports itself. When a screen crashed, members
  saw the reload screen and nobody was told. That crash is now recorded with the
  highest severity, naming the page that died.
- Quieter, faster, and more honest throughout. 68 distinct conditions across the
  app now identify themselves precisely instead of failing silently — covering
  uploads, comments, sign-in, notifications, judging and the admin tools.

