   no notification icon existed anywhere in the repository, so the messaging
   library fell back to the launcher icon - and since Android 5.0 the status
   bar flattens the small icon to its alpha mask, keeping only which pixels
   are solid. An opaque square becomes a solid white rectangle.

   The owner's logo now ships as the mark, cut separately at each of the five
   densities. The build opens the finished bundle and FAILS if the icon or
   either manifest entry is missing, so this cannot silently regress.

2. 74 CORRUPTED CHARACTERS REPAIRED  (new since 1041)

   A UTF-8 file had been read as Latin-1 and re-saved, turning single
   characters into two or three. 41 of them rendered to members as empty
   boxes:

     - every competition placement badge (trophy, medals, mentions, stars)
     - every round status icon (tick, star, cross, warning)
     - the sidebar medal icons
     - four sidebar links that should end in an arrow
     - the pinned-comment marker
     - both comment box placeholders
     - the unvote warning, which should read "2x the original reward"

   Repaired by reversing the exact byte transformation, not by retyping. A
   test now fails the build if it ever returns.

3. THE COMMENT SEND BUTTON  (new since 1041)

   Measured on production: the send button was a 24x24 px tap target. The
   minimum on Android is 48dp and on iOS 44pt, and an adult thumb is about
   45px across - so the target was smaller than the finger meant to hit it.
   People were missing it and hitting the text field instead.

   It is now 44x44. The icon is unchanged at 16px, so nothing looks
   different - there is simply something to hit. It also fires on pointer
   down as well as click, because the Android WebView can fail to deliver a
   click after a tap that closes the keyboard, and the keyboard now shows a
   Send key instead of a plain newline.

