REGISTRATION — the one thing this build must not break, and does not
- A new member was stopped dead at the last step of signing up by
  "Upload failed / Please try another image" with no reason given. A profile
  photo is mandatory, so they could not join at all.
  Cause: the image loader rejected its promise with a DOM Event, which has no
  `.message`, so every caller printed its fallback string. The upload never
  reached the network - the browser could not decode the chosen file.
  Fixed: a real error carrying the file's type (to the console, never to the
  member), a second decode attempt via createImageBitmap that rescues files the
  <img> element rejects, and a message that says what to do next without naming
  any format or vendor.
- The signup gate itself is UNCHANGED: 18+, a profile photo on our own storage,
  an available username, a member type, and at least one interest. Each has its
  own specific message. Nothing was added to it.
- Server changes shipped today do not affect app versions already on Play:
  1033/1034 never called the new functions, the grouped-history function's
  signature is untouched, and the SELECT policy behind their notification list
  is unchanged.

NOTIFICATIONS - the system, rebuilt
- The panel that would not close. framer-motion kept the exiting node mounted:
  a 304x456 invisible rectangle over the top-right of every page, swallowing
  clicks until reload. On Android it simply stayed visible over the new page.
  Removal no longer waits on an animation; a route change, Escape, an outside
  tap and a real backdrop each close it independently.
- The chime played twice on every arrival - the bell is mounted twice, one copy
  hidden by CSS, and CSS hides without unmounting. Exactly one instance now owns
  the subscription and the sound, and leadership moves if that copy unmounts.
- One sentence everywhere. The bell used to render frozen text written by the
  database months earlier while the history page recomposed its own. Same event,
  different words. Both now come from one function.
- Push said "commented on your post" while the app said "commented on your
  photo". The push body is composed at send time now, from live data. It also
  stops naming 33 members who have deleted their accounts, and an admin can no
  longer appear under a real person's name.
- The badge stopped counting at 30. It counted a page, not the inbox; a member
  with 111 unread saw 30. It counts every unread event now, and the panel says
  how many are not on screen instead of quietly stopping.
- The bell groups like the history page - a day of reactions is one line, with
  real counts, not 40 lines.
- Tapping a new-post notification landed you on the dashboard. It opens the post.
  A reply opened an unrelated gallery. It opens the post.
- A friend request was counted twice and drawn twice. Once now. Answering one
  also clears the notification behind it.
- Push notifications can be turned off - a master switch plus per-type switches,
  including the new-photo alerts, which are the most frequent.
- A notification can be deleted. Until now nothing in the app could remove one.
- Notifications older than 90 days are cleared automatically. Anything still
  unread is kept, however old.
- The history screen is reachable from the account menu on phone and desktop.
  It used to be reachable only from inside a panel that closes itself.

